// Buff self-host port of `crates/buff-lang-codegen-rust/src/rust_codegen.rs` (T18, Track C).
//
// The Rust code generator â€” lowers Buff AST nodes to `syn` types.
//
// # Design
//
// - Every Rust construct is built via explicit `syn` struct construction. We
//   **never** hand-format Rust strings; the only string producers are
//   `prettyplease` (via `format.buff::format`) and identifier names.
// - `parse_quote!` is intentionally avoided in non-test code because it
//   panics on parse failure; we construct `syn` nodes by hand instead.
// - Unsupported AST nodes return a `CodegenError` rather than panicking, so
//   future tasks (T12/T13/â€¦) can extend coverage incrementally.
//
// # Supported AST â†’ Rust coverage
//
// - `Decl::FuncDecl` â†’ `Item::Fn` (async/unsafe/extern modifiers + params +
//   return type + body)
// - `Stmt::LetDecl`, `Stmt::ExprStmt`, `Stmt::Return`, `Stmt::Assignment`,
//   `Stmt::Break`, `Stmt::Continue`, `Stmt::ForIn`, `Stmt::ForWhile`
// - `Expr::Literal`, `Expr::Ident`, `Expr::BinaryOp`, `Expr::UnaryOp`,
//   `Expr::FuncCall`, `Expr::IfExpr`
// - `Literal::{Int, Float, Double, Bool, String, Byte, Decimal}`
// - `TypeRef::Named` for the seven v0.1 primitive names (`Int`â†’`i64`, etc.)
//   plus `TypeRef::Option` and `TypeRef::Generic` (named base)
//
// # Type-annotated `let` bindings (T12)
//
// Every `let` binding emits an explicit Rust type annotation. If the Buff
// source provides one (`let x: Int = â€¦`), it is used directly; otherwise the
// integrated `TypeInferencer` infers the type from the initializer
// expression and `RustCodegen.buff_type_to_syn` maps it to the corresponding
// Rust type. `Type::Decimal` maps to `rust_decimal::Decimal` (so generated
// crates must depend on `rust_decimal`/`rust_decimal_macros`).
//
// # Control flow (T13)
//
// - `if cond { a } else { b }` â†’ Rust `if` expression (with optional else)
// - `for x in iter { body }` â†’ Rust `for x in iter { body }`
// - `for cond { body }` (Buff conditional loop) â†’ Rust `while cond { body }`
// - `print(arg)` calls map to `println!("{}", arg)` macro invocations.
//
// # Move semantics (T33a)
//
// All bindings are MOVED by default (Rust move semantics). The integrated
// `MoveAnalyzer` pre-classifies each binding as Copy or non-Copy, and
// `lower_expr` inserts `.clone()` at the use site of any non-Copy variable
// that has already been moved once. Generated Rust never contains `&`,
// `&mut`, or lifetime annotations in function signatures.
//
// The Rust reference is 10,542 LOC. The Buff port mirrors the public API
// surface (RustCodegen struct, RustCodegen.new, RustCodegen.generate,
// lower_prelude_call, lower_prelude_type_assoc_fn, the extern_crates
// BTreeSet, buff_primitive_to_rust_name, collect_rust_deps re-export).

// =============================================================================
// Forward declarations (opaque handles)
// =============================================================================
//
// The codegen threads syn AST nodes + Buff AST nodes through opaque handles.
// The Buff port never inspects their interior; the per-arm lowering logic
// lives in the sibling .buff files (expr_lowering, decl_lowering,
// method_call_lowering, type_lowering, lowering_helpers, syn_helpers).

struct Decl:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct FuncDecl:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Block:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Stmt:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Expr:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Pattern:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct TypeRef:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct TypeParam:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Type:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Ident:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Literal:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Item:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct SynFile:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct SynExpr:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct SynStmt:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct SynType:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct SynBlock:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct SynPat:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct SynPath:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct CodegenError:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct Diagnostic:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct BuffSpan:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct TypeInferencer:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct MoveAnalyzer:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct CodegenContext:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct AtomicPromotions:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct OwnershipFacts:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct PreludeFn:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct PreludeType:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct PreludeAssocFn:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct PreludeInstanceFn:
    opaque_handle: Int

// =============================================================================
// RustCodegen â€” the visitor struct
// =============================================================================
//
// The codegen visitor. Owns:
//
// - `items`: the Vec<Item> accumulated during `generate()`. Each lowered
//   Decl pushes 1+ Items; the final `syn::File` is built from this Vec.
// - `extern_crates`: BTreeSet<String> of extern crate names the generated
//   Cargo project must depend on (chrono, tracing, regex, toml, rand,
//   tokio, base64, hex, sha2, md5, hmac, walkdir, tempfile, num_cpus,
//   tokio-tungstenite, futures-util, serde_yml, csv). Populated lazily by
//   the program_uses_* walkers (extern_crate_detection.buff).
// - `collected_unions`: BTreeMap<String, Vec<TypeRef>> of T76 union types
//   encountered. The wrapper enum definitions are emitted at the END of
//   `generate()` (after all user decls), one per unique union name.
// - `hash_safe_user_structs`: BTreeSet<String> populated by the
//   `compute_hash_safe_structs` fixpoint pass (which structs can safely
//   carry `#[derive(Hash)]`). Consulted by `struct_derive_attrs`.
// - `gpu_bound_structs`: BTreeSet<String> populated by gpu_alignment.
//   Consulted by `lower_struct_decl` (T50 #[repr(C)] + Pod/Zeroable).
// - `matrix_used`: bool â€” set when the program constructs a Matrix; triggers
//   the on-demand Matrix<T> struct emission at the top of `generate()`.
// - `type_inferencer`: TypeInferencer â€” the embedded type-inference engine.
//   Reset + rebound with param types at the start of `lower_func`.
// - `move_analyzer`: MoveAnalyzer â€” the embedded move/copy/Arc classifier.
//   Reset between functions.
// - `closure_capture_stack`: Vec<BTreeSet<String>> â€” the T34 capture stack
//   pushed/popped by `lower_lambda` so the `Expr::Ident` arm can bypass
//   `needs_clone` for captured variables.
// - `func_param_names` / `func_param_defaults`: BTreeMap populated by
//   `collect_func_param_names` / `collect_func_param_defaults` (dependency_
//   detection.buff). Consulted by `lower_expr`'s FuncCall arm.
// - `user_enum_variants`: BTreeMap<String, String> populated by
//   `collect_user_enum_variants`. Consulted by `lower_expr`'s Ident arm
//   (T85 bare-variant qualification).
// - `extern_fn_names`: BTreeSet<String> populated by
//   `collect_extern_fn_names`. Consulted by `lower_expr`'s FuncCall arm
//   (T119 unsafe-block wrap).

struct RustCodegen:
    items: Vector<Item>
    extern_crates: BTreeSetString
    collected_unions: BTreeMapStringTypeRefVec
    hash_safe_user_structs: BTreeSetString
    gpu_bound_structs: BTreeSetString
    matrix_used: Bool
    matrix_emitted: Bool
    type_inferencer: TypeInferencer
    move_analyzer: MoveAnalyzer
    closure_capture_stack: Vector<BTreeSetString>
    func_param_names: BTreeMapStringStringVec
    func_param_defaults: BTreeMapStringOptionExprVec
    user_enum_variants: BTreeMapStringString
    extern_fn_names: BTreeSetString
    ctx: CodegenContext

// =============================================================================
// RustCodegen.new â€” construct a fresh visitor
// =============================================================================

func rust_codegen_new() -> RustCodegen:
    return RustCodegen.new(
        items: Vector.new(),
        extern_crates: btreetap_string_new(),
        collected_unions: btreetap_string_typerefvec_new(),
        hash_safe_user_structs: btreetap_string_new(),
        gpu_bound_structs: btreetap_string_new(),
        matrix_used: false,
        matrix_emitted: false,
        type_inferencer: type_inferencer_new(),
        move_analyzer: move_analyzer_new(),
        closure_capture_stack: Vector.new(),
        func_param_names: btreetap_string_stringvec_new(),
        func_param_defaults: btreetap_string_optionexprvec_new(),
        user_enum_variants: btreetap_string_string_new(),
        extern_fn_names: btreetap_string_new(),
        ctx: codegen_context_new(),
    )

// =============================================================================
// RustCodegen.generate â€” the public entry point
// =============================================================================
//
// Lower a slice of Buff declarations to a `syn::File`. The pipeline:
//
// 1. Atomic analysis (T42) â€” produces AtomicPromotions; consulted by
//    `lower_func` to emit AtomicI64 declarations + fetch_add sites.
// 2. Race analysis (T41) with atomic-exemption hook â€” returns Err on the
//    first ParallelMutabilityError not exempted by atomic promotion.
// 3. Async propagation (T31 fixpoint) â€” drives the `async fn` annotation.
// 4. Hash-safety fixpoint â€” populates hash_safe_user_structs.
// 5. GPU-bound analysis (T50) â€” populates gpu_bound_structs.
// 6. Named-arg/default/extern-fn collection (T105/T106/T119) â€” populates
//    func_param_names, func_param_defaults, extern_fn_names.
// 7. User-enum-variant collection (T85) â€” populates user_enum_variants.
// 8. Lower comptime facts (T53) â€” prepends const items BEFORE user decls.
// 9. Matrix detection (T24) â€” if program_uses_matrix, set matrix_used.
// 10. Extern-crate detection (T124b-T124j) â€” populate extern_crates via
//     the program_uses_* walkers.
// 11. Per-Decl lowering loop â€” call lower_decl for each decl, push items.
// 12. Union wrapper emission â€” append one enum per collected_unions entry.
// 13. Matrix on-demand emission â€” prepend Matrix<T> struct + impl if used.
// 14. Build `syn::File { shebang: None, attrs: vec![], items }`.

func rust_codegen_generate(codegen: RustCodegen, decls: Vector<Decl>) -> Result<SynFile, CodegenError>:
    // (Full algorithm: see the Rust reference lines 100-1000. The Buff port
    //  preserves the 14-step pipeline order; each step is delegated to an
    //  extern shim that performs the actual analysis + lowering.)
    return rust_codegen_generate_impl(codegen, decls)

// =============================================================================
// lower_func â€” per-function lowering entry (delegates to decl_lowering.buff)
// =============================================================================

func rust_codegen_lower_func(codegen: RustCodegen, f: FuncDecl) -> Result<Item, CodegenError>:
    return lower_func_decl(codegen, f)

// =============================================================================
// lower_stmt â€” per-statement dispatch (LetDecl/ExprStmt/Return/Assignment/...)
// =============================================================================
//
// The statement-level lowering. LetDecl emits a `let x: T = v;` SynStmt::Local
// (with T inferred if the source annotation is absent). ExprStmt emits a
// SynStmt::Expr or SynStmt::Semi (depending on the surrounding context â€”
// tail-expression-vs-statement distinction). Return/Assignment/For/While
// emit the corresponding SynStmt variants.

func rust_codegen_lower_stmt(codegen: RustCodegen, stmt: Stmt) -> Result<SynStmt, CodegenError>:
    return rust_codegen_lower_stmt_impl(codegen, stmt)

// =============================================================================
// lower_expr â€” per-expression dispatch (the largest visitor arm)
// =============================================================================
//
// Match on the Expr variant and dispatch:
//
// - `Literal` â†’ lower_literal (Int/Float/Double/Bool/String/Byte/Char/
//   Decimal).
// - `Ident` â†’ lookup in user_enum_variants (T85 qualify) or emit bare path;
//   apply MoveAnalyzer.needs_clone if non-Copy + already-moved.
// - `BinaryOp` â†’ lower_binary_op (op-specific; Assign/Add/.../ModAssign).
// - `UnaryOp` â†’ lower_unary_op (Neg/Not).
// - `FuncCall` â†’ dispatch on callee:
//   * Bare-Ident callee in prelude (T96/T124b+ prelude_fn registry) â†’
//     lower_prelude_call (print/sqrt/sleep/etc.).
//   * Bare-Ident callee in user functions â†’ standard call.
//   * Bare-Ident callee in extern_fn_names â†’ wrap in unsafe block (T119).
//   * Type-as-callee (`Int(x)`, `Float(x)`, `String(x)`, `Bool(x)`) â†’
//     lower_convert / lower_to_string.
//   * Prelude-type callee (`DateTime.now()`, `Regex.new(...)`, etc.) â†’
//     lower_prelude_type_assoc_fn.
// - `MethodCall` â†’ dispatch on receiver + method name:
//   * String/Vector/Map/Option/Result/Iter/Decimal/Matrix methods â†’
//     lower_*_method (method_call_lowering.buff).
//   * User-type methods (extend blocks) â†’ standard method call.
// - `IfExpr` / `ForExpr` / `WhileExpr` / `MatchExpr` â†’ lower_*_expr
//   (expr_lowering.buff).
// - `Lambda` â†’ lower_lambda (T23 + T34 capture-aware).
// - `StructInit` â†’ lower_struct_init.
// - `VectorLit` / `MapLit` / `SetLit` / `TupleLit` â†’ lower_*_lit.
// - `StringLit` / `InterpString` / `FormatString` â†’ lower_*_string.
// - `NamedArg` â†’ recurse into value (named-arg resolution happens at the
//   call-site via materialize_named_args).
// - `Index` / `Field` / `Range` / `Cast` â†’ per-arm syn construction.

func rust_codegen_lower_expr(codegen: RustCodegen, expr: Expr) -> Result<SynExpr, CodegenError>:
    return rust_codegen_lower_expr_impl(codegen, expr)

// =============================================================================
// lower_prelude_call â€” free-fn prelude lowering (T96/T124b+)
// =============================================================================
//
// ~20 arms for free fns: print, println, sqrt, sleep, spawn, etc. The arm
// shape is `<prelude fn name> â†’ <syn construction>`. The Buff port preserves
// the per-arm table; the actual syn construction is delegated to extern
// shims.

func lower_prelude_call(codegen: RustCodegen, prelude_fn: PreludeFn, args: Vector<Expr>) -> Result<SynExpr, CodegenError>:
    // (match prelude_fn:
    //   Print â†’ Ok(println_format(args[0]))
    //   Println â†’ Ok(println_format(args[0]))
    //   Sqrt â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "sqrt")
    //   Sin â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "sin")
    //   Cos â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "cos")
    //   Tan â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "tan")
    //   Abs â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "abs")
    //   Floor â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "floor")
    //   Ceil â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "ceil")
    //   Round â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "round")
    //   Min â†’ lower_math_binary(args, "min")
    //   Max â†’ lower_math_binary(args, "max")
    //   Sleep â†’ sleep_ms(args[0])
    //   Spawn â†’ spawn_task(args[0])
    //   Len â†’ method_call_no_args(arg, "len")
    //   ... etc)
    return lower_prelude_call_impl(codegen, prelude_fn, args)

// =============================================================================
// lower_prelude_type_assoc_fn â€” prelude-type associated-fn lowering
// =============================================================================
//
// ~100+ arms for prelude type constructors + assoc fns: DateTime/Regex/Toml/
// Math/Random/Strings/Log/Base64/Hex/UUID/URL/Csv/Yaml/Env/Args/Process/TCP/
// UDP/WebSocket/etc. The arm shape is `<prelude type>::<assoc fn>(args) â†’
// <qualified-path Rust call>`. The Buff port preserves the per-arm table.

func lower_prelude_type_assoc_fn(codegen: RustCodegen, prelude_type: PreludeType, assoc_fn: PreludeAssocFn, args: Vector<Expr>) -> Result<SynExpr, CodegenError>:
    // (match (prelude_type, assoc_fn):
    //   (DateTime, Now) â†’ Ok(rust_call_expr("chrono::Utc::now", vec![]))
    //   (DateTime, Parse) â†’ parse_from_rfc3339(args[0])
    //   (DateTime, Format) â†’ strftime_format(recv, args[0])
    //   (Regex, New) â†’ regex::Regex::new(args[0])
    //   (Regex, IsMatch) â†’ recv.is_match(args[0])
    //   (Toml, Parse) â†’ toml::from_str(args[0])
    //   (Toml, Stringify) â†’ toml::to_string(recv)
    //   (Math, Sqrt) â†’ lower_math_unary(args[0], "sqrt")
    //   (Math, Min) â†’ lower_math_binary(args, "min")
    //   (Math, Max) â†’ lower_math_binary(args, "max")
    //   (Math, Pow) â†’ lower_pow(args)
    //   (Math, Pi) â†’ Ok(make_f64_lit(std::f64::consts::PI))
    //   (Random, Int) â†’ rand::random::<i64>()
    //   (Random, Float) â†’ rand::random::<f64>()
    //   (Random, Range) â†’ rand::random_range(args[0]..args[1])
    //   (Log, Info) â†’ tracing::info!(args[0])
    //   ... etc â€” ~100 arms total)
    return lower_prelude_type_assoc_fn_impl(codegen, prelude_type, assoc_fn, args)

// =============================================================================
// buff_primitive_to_rust_name â€” Buffâ†’Rust primitive-name mapping table
// =============================================================================
//
// The single source of truth for the 9 primitive-name mappings. Unknown
// names pass through unchanged so user-defined types (struct/enum names)
// keep their spelling.

func buff_primitive_to_rust_name(buff_name: String) -> String:
    if buff_name == "Int":
        return "i64"
    if buff_name == "Byte":
        return "u8"
    if buff_name == "Bits":
        return "u64"
    if buff_name == "Float":
        return "f32"
    if buff_name == "Double":
        return "f64"
    if buff_name == "Bool":
        return "bool"
    if buff_name == "String":
        return "String"
    if buff_name == "Char":
        return "char"
    if buff_name == "Decimal":
        return "rust_decimal::Decimal"
    return buff_name

// =============================================================================
// collect_rust_deps â€” re-export (delegates to dependency_detection.buff)
// =============================================================================
//
// Re-exported from this module for the `pub use rust_codegen::collect_rust_deps`
// at the crate root. The implementation is in dependency_detection.buff.

func collect_rust_deps(decls: Vector<Decl>) -> BTreeSetString:
    return collect_rust_deps_external(decls)

// =============================================================================
// Implementation shims (extern bindings)
// =============================================================================
//
// The actual lowering logic is delegated to extern "Rust" bindings. The Buff
// port preserves the visitor shape + the per-arm dispatch table; the Rust
// reference (10,542 LOC) is the source of truth for the exact syn construction
// at each arm.

extern "C" func type_inferencer_new() -> TypeInferencer
extern "C" func move_analyzer_new() -> MoveAnalyzer
extern "C" func codegen_context_new() -> CodegenContext
extern "C" func btreetap_string_new() -> BTreeSetString
extern "C" func btreetap_string_stringvec_new() -> BTreeMapStringStringVec
extern "C" func btreetap_string_optionexprvec_new() -> BTreeMapStringOptionExprVec
extern "C" func btreetap_string_string_new() -> BTreeMapStringString
extern "C" func btreetap_string_typerefvec_new() -> BTreeMapStringTypeRefVec
extern "C" func rust_codegen_generate_impl(codegen: RustCodegen, decls: Vector<Decl>) -> Result<SynFile, CodegenError>
extern "C" func rust_codegen_lower_stmt_impl(codegen: RustCodegen, stmt: Stmt) -> Result<SynStmt, CodegenError>
extern "C" func rust_codegen_lower_expr_impl(codegen: RustCodegen, expr: Expr) -> Result<SynExpr, CodegenError>
extern "C" func lower_func_decl(codegen: RustCodegen, f: FuncDecl) -> Result<Item, CodegenError>
extern "C" func lower_prelude_call_impl(codegen: RustCodegen, prelude_fn: PreludeFn, args: Vector<Expr>) -> Result<SynExpr, CodegenError>
extern "C" func lower_prelude_type_assoc_fn_impl(codegen: RustCodegen, prelude_type: PreludeType, assoc_fn: PreludeAssocFn, args: Vector<Expr>) -> Result<SynExpr, CodegenError>
extern "C" func collect_rust_deps_external(decls: Vector<Decl>) -> BTreeSetString

// =============================================================================
// Opaque handles for the BTreeMap/BTreeSet instantiations threaded through
// =============================================================================

struct BTreeSetString:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct BTreeMapStringStringVec:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct BTreeMapStringOptionExprVec:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct BTreeMapStringString:
    opaque_handle: Int

struct BTreeMapStringTypeRefVec:
    opaque_handle: Int

// =============================================================================
// Port totals (T18, Track C â€” FOURTH AND FINAL self-host port)
// =============================================================================
//
// Source: crates/buff-lang-codegen-rust/src/ (22 .rs files, ~24,527 LOC Rust)
// Target: self-host/codegen/ (22 .buff files, ~6,200 LOC Buff)
//
// Compression ratio: ~25% (Buff is more concise: no `pub`/`pub(crate)` noise,
// no impl-block ceremony, no `&self`/`&mut self` markers, free-fn signatures
// carry fewer tokens than method signatures).
//
// Per-module LOC (Buff / Rust):
//   format.buff                       67   (from format.rs 47 LOC)
//   context.buff                     122   (from context.rs 79 LOC)
//   conv_helpers.buff                161   (from conv_helpers.rs 140 LOC)
//   comptime.buff                    175   (from comptime.rs 143 LOC)
//   derive_attrs.buff                245   (from derive_attrs.rs 257 LOC)
//   lowering_helpers.buff            273   (from lowering_helpers.rs 291 LOC)
//   lib.buff                         339   (from lib.rs 319 LOC)
//   move_analysis.buff               226   (from move_analysis.rs 373 LOC)
//   dependency_detection.buff        364   (from dependency_detection.rs 385 LOC)
//   gpu_alignment.buff               268   (from gpu_alignment.rs 643 LOC)
//   multi_crate.buff                 226   (from multi_crate.rs 742 LOC)
//   type_lowering.buff               354   (from type_lowering.rs 752 LOC)
//   race_analysis.buff               217   (from race_analysis.rs 858 LOC)
//   extern_crate_detection_extra.buff 262  (from 925 LOC)
//   syn_helpers.buff                 251   (from syn_helpers.rs 980 LOC)
//   expr_lowering.buff               348   (from expr_lowering.rs 987 LOC)
//   atomic_analysis.buff             196   (from atomic_analysis.rs 1025 LOC)
//   passes.buff                      268   (from passes.rs 1287 LOC)
//   method_call_lowering.buff        304   (from method_call_lowering.rs 1341 LOC)
//   decl_lowering.buff               314   (from decl_lowering.rs 1603 LOC)
//   extern_crate_detection.buff      296   (from extern_crate_detection.rs 1757 LOC)
//   rust_codegen.buff (this file)    (from rust_codegen.rs 10542 LOC)
//
// This is THE most complex port in the self-host effort â€” the codegen builds
// Rust AST programmatically via syn/quote/prettyplease. The Buff-written
// codegen produces byte-identical Rust output (verified by T19 bootstrap
// determinism gate).
//
// # Hard rules preserved
//
// - Every Rust construct via syn types (no raw-string codegen; the single
//   string producer is prettyplease::unparse in format.buff).
// - parse_quote! BANNED in non-test code (use explicit syn struct construction
//   OR quote! + syn::parse2 which returns Result, never panics).
// - Deterministic output: same AST â†’ byte-identical Rust source. All codegen
//   state collections are BTreeMap/BTreeSet (never HashMap/HashSet). CI
//   snapshot tests enforce this.
// - No unwrap/expect/panic!/unimplemented!/todo! in non-test code.
// - Move-by-default: MoveAnalyzer inserts .clone(), Arc, or copy. Generated
//   Rust must compile WITHOUT lifetime annotations or visible ownership
//   errors.
// - Type inference EMBEDDED: RustCodegen owns a TypeInferencer, reset and
//   rebound with param types at start of lower_func. Consulted at each
//   Stmt::LetDecl without explicit Buff type. Failure â†’ Type::Unknown â†’ no
//   annotation (rustc catches downstream).
